    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27281" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lŭtātĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Luctātĭus</span></b> ), a, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a
			Roman</i> gens. So, Q. Lutatius Catulus, <i>consul</i> A. U. C. 652, <i><span class="en">Cic. Mur. 17, 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Cael.
				29, 70</span></i>; <i>a younger man of the same name,
				consul</i> A. U. C. 676, <i><span class="en">id. Cat.
				3, 10, 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Balb. 15, 34</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lŭtātĭānus
			(Luct-</span></b> ), a, um, <i>adj., of</i>
			or <i>belonging to a Lutatius, Lutatian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					33, 1, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
